SUMMARY:Trench Innovation Sprint: Lunch-and-Learn Info Session
DESCRIPTION:Abstract \nCalling all U of T ECE and MIE students: Join Lawson Climate Institute for the Trench Canada and Hydro One Innovation Sprint! \nThe Innovation Sprint is open to University of Toronto students enrolled in programs at The Edward S. Rogers Sr. Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering and the Department of Mechanical & Industrial Engineering at undergraduate\, Master’s\, and PhD levels. Participants are invited to join us for a Lunch & Learn\, networking\, and team formation session on October 5\, 2026\, where teams of 3 to 5 students will be formed. Teams will then develop their solutions ahead of the Final Presentations and Awards on October 21\, 2026. \nEach member of winning teams will receive a prize! Prizes may include: \n\n$1\,000 Amazon gift card\n$750 Amazon gift card\n$500 Amazon gift card\nApple Watch\nAirPods\n\nThis opportunity is presented by Trench Canada and Hydro One in collaboration with the University of Toronto’s Lawson Climate Institute. \nPre-registration is required by September 30 to enjoy this free event. \nRegister
URL:https://www.engineering.utoronto.ca/event/trench-innovation-sprint-lunch-and-learn-info-session/
LOCATION:Lawson Centre for Sustainability\, 25 Devonshire Place\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M5S 2C8\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Lectures, seminars and workshops
END:VEVENT
